# Hearth COSMIC on Anatase (Fedora): what os-bases/anatase/build.sh and cosmic-test.yml install. One package a line;
# lines starting with "-" are left out (--exclude). docs/COSMIC.md says why each is or isn't here.
# COSMIC's workspace
cosmic-session
cosmic-comp
cosmic-panel
cosmic-settings
cosmic-settings-daemon
cosmic-launcher
cosmic-applets
cosmic-bg
cosmic-osd
cosmic-notifications
cosmic-workspaces
cosmic-app-library
cosmic-randr
cosmic-idle
cosmic-icon-theme
xdg-desktop-portal-cosmic
# COSMIC's own apps for the kinds it has (in COSMIC they take the place of Hearth Files, Terminal and Text)
cosmic-files
cosmic-term
cosmic-edit
# Fedora's cosmic-session can't be installed without these. They're installed but never used: COSMIC's login screen
# (cosmic-greeter, greetd) isn't switched on (Anatase's stays; build.sh checks the display manager didn't change), the
# first-run wizard's autostart entry is removed, and Hearth's on-screen keyboard is the one on the controller.
cosmic-osk
cosmic-greeter
cosmic-initial-setup
# Left out: apps of kinds Hearth already has, and COSMIC's wallpapers (Hearth's Fireside is used)
-cosmic-store
-cosmic-player
-cosmic-wallpapers
-cosmic-monitor
